==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[File:1 TND - 1980 - obverse.jpg|thumb|A note worth one Tunisian '''dinar''', which may itself be referred to as a '''dinar'''.]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|ar|en}} {{m|ar|دِينَار}} and {{etyl|sh|en}} {{m|sh|динар}} (which is also from the Arabic), derived from the {{etyl|la|en}} {{m|la|dēnārius}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{a|UK}} {{IPA|/ˈdiːnɑː(ɹ)/|lang=en}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# Name of official [[currency]] of several countries, including [[Algeria]], [[Bahrain]], [[Iraq]], [[Jordan]], [[Kuwait]], [[Libya]], [[Serbia]] and [[Tunisia]].
# A coin or note worth one dinar.

